  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In order to measure the internal resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;of a cell of emf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;a meter bridge of wire resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>, a resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, another cell of emf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(internal resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>) and a galvanometer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math>&nbsp;are used in a circuit, as shown in the figure. If the null point is found at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>72</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0002_679cda183f8a.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 155px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0002_595b538ddf31.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 241px;\" /></p><p>Resistance of potential wire is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Resistance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;wire&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>So, Resistance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;wire&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>50</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>72</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Current,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>&#949;</mi></mstyle><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#949;</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>75</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
  }
